    "synopsis": {
        "native": "Louis c'est ce mec super gentil. Et dans son cabinet d'avocat, ce n'est pas un compliment. Le jour o\u00f9 son m\u00e9decin lui diagnostique par erreur une maladie grave, le regard des autres change : on fait attention \u00e0 lui, on lui pose des questions et on \u00e9coute les r\u00e9ponses, Louis existe enfin ! Alors bien \u00e9videmment, il h\u00e9site \u00e0 dire qu'il va tr\u00e8s bien.",
        "english": "Louis is so nice that nobody notices him. He is, in fact, missing out on his own life. The day he believes he has cancer, people around him seem to care about him for the first time, and personal and professional opportunities come pouring in. His law firm requires him to defend a multinational company accused of causing cancer by a group of affected patients. Louis discovers that existence has a price, the price of lying."
